<PageTitle>Groot.UI — Progress concepts</PageTitle>

<div class="ds">
    <header class="ds-head">
        <h1 class="g-serif">Progress<span class="accent">.</span></h1>
        <p class="sub">
            Four ways to draw the same five years: a thin 2025 with a long gap, a strong 2027, one
            joker week and one record. Every concept reads the same sample data at the same scale,
            so what differs on screen is the drawing and not the numbers.
        </p>
        <p class="sub">
            The name is the loose end. "Year rings" came from tree rings, survived the pass that
            took the plant language out because it read as abstract, and then the drawing under it
            became plates three days later. None of the four below is a ring.
        </p>
        <p class="sub">
            Background: <code>Plan/progress-year-rings-screen.md</code> holds the decision and its
            2026-08-21 update, and <code>design/habit-system.md</code> §4 has Concept C. Weights
            are kilograms throughout, which is what the rest of the app speaks.
        </p>
    </header>

